WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:01.201
Welcome back to a special

00:00:01.201 --> 00:00:02.035
edition of OUTFRONT.

00:00:02.035 --> 00:00:03.870
We are live in Ukraine tonight.

00:00:03.870 --> 00:00:04.971
This country at war.

00:00:04.971 --> 00:00:06.740
For now. 16 months.

00:00:06.740 --> 00:00:09.642
And when or if this war ends

00:00:10.076 --> 00:00:11.511
what comes next?

00:00:11.511 --> 00:00:13.680
Well, for a small view of that, today,

00:00:13.680 --> 00:00:15.315
we went back to a town

00:00:15.315 --> 00:00:16.182
that we visited

00:00:16.182 --> 00:00:18.351
near the start of the war.

00:00:20.220 --> 00:00:21.688
This is the village of Andriivka.

00:00:21.688 --> 00:00:24.190
It was attacked and occupied by Russians.

00:00:24.190 --> 00:00:26.026
It was the most destroyed village

00:00:26.026 --> 00:00:27.127
in the entire

00:00:27.127 --> 00:00:28.395
region of Kiev,

00:00:28.395 --> 00:00:30.797
just destroyed by relentless shelling.

00:00:30.797 --> 00:00:33.099
Today, it looks quite different.

00:00:33.099 --> 00:00:34.501
There's been a lot of rebuilding.

00:00:34.501 --> 00:00:35.902
And one of the people

00:00:35.902 --> 00:00:37.637
who's been doing a lot of it.

00:00:37.637 --> 00:00:39.706
So much of the cleanup is Olga.

00:00:39.706 --> 00:00:41.441
You may remember Olga and Vadim.

00:00:41.441 --> 00:00:44.110
We were at their house last year.

00:00:44.110 --> 00:00:45.445
This was the cellar,

00:00:45.445 --> 00:00:47.447
the root cellar where they stayed

00:00:47.447 --> 00:00:49.082
while the Russians were occupying

00:00:49.082 --> 00:00:51.151
and staying in foxholes in the back.

00:00:51.151 --> 00:00:52.352
This whole area was covered

00:00:52.352 --> 00:00:54.487
with pieces of rockets and shells,

00:00:54.888 --> 00:00:56.489
ordnance, ammunition.

00:00:56.489 --> 00:00:58.625
This was the house over a year ago.

00:00:58.658 --> 00:00:59.359
Walking through it,

00:00:59.359 --> 00:01:00.460
it was completely destroyed.

00:01:00.460 --> 00:01:02.562
But now it's leveled now.

00:01:02.829 --> 00:01:04.898
Olga and Vadim are divorced.

00:01:05.298 --> 00:01:07.834
It's another casualty of this war.

00:01:08.435 --> 00:01:11.071
And Olga has confirmed that her son,

00:01:11.071 --> 00:01:14.007
her only child, died fighting for Keith.

00:01:14.841 --> 00:01:16.176
It's something she lives with

00:01:16.176 --> 00:01:17.744
every single day.

00:01:17.744 --> 00:01:19.112
She lives here alone.

00:01:19.112 --> 00:01:20.313
And she says she is committed

00:01:20.313 --> 00:01:21.448
to staying here.

00:01:21.448 --> 00:01:23.016
She says 20% of the village is gone

00:01:23.016 --> 00:01:24.451
and is never going to come back.

00:01:24.451 --> 00:01:26.519
But she's going to stay here and rebuild.

00:01:26.519 --> 00:01:27.120
She describes

00:01:27.120 --> 00:01:27.754
it is doing her own

00:01:27.754 --> 00:01:30.023
small part to rebuild this country

00:01:30.757 --> 00:01:31.858
for her lost son.

00:01:33.026 --> 00:01:34.327
This is where she lives now.

00:01:34.327 --> 00:01:36.062
She said a local businessman

00:01:36.062 --> 00:01:38.031
donated about 13 of these structures

00:01:38.031 --> 00:01:39.365
to people in the town.

00:01:39.365 --> 00:01:40.934
And this is their temporary.

00:01:40.934 --> 00:01:41.601
But this is,

00:01:41.601 --> 00:01:42.102
as she said,

00:01:42.102 --> 00:01:42.769
pretty much going to be

00:01:42.769 --> 00:01:44.270
her permanent home.

00:01:44.270 --> 00:01:45.472
As she works

00:01:45.472 --> 00:01:46.773
again, she describes in her own

00:01:46.773 --> 00:01:48.942
small way to rebuild.

00:01:48.942 --> 00:01:49.876
She grows

00:01:49.876 --> 00:01:51.111
all of her own food,

00:01:51.111 --> 00:01:53.146
her fruits and vegetables in the back,

00:01:53.146 --> 00:01:55.648
growing them right on top of the foxholes

00:01:56.216 --> 00:01:58.351
where the Russians were living.

00:01:58.418 --> 00:01:59.486
Here's the garden

00:01:59.486 --> 00:02:02.489
now full of fruits, vegetables, birdsong.

00:02:03.056 --> 00:02:05.058
The foxholes here are filled in.

00:02:05.058 --> 00:02:05.692
But a year ago,

00:02:05.692 --> 00:02:06.292
of course,

00:02:06.292 --> 00:02:08.261
they were here with mattresses

00:02:08.261 --> 00:02:09.596
that the Russians stole

00:02:09.596 --> 00:02:12.332
from the Ukrainians makeshift chimneys.

00:02:12.899 --> 00:02:14.300
The Russians in their foxholes

00:02:14.300 --> 00:02:15.368
were living a lot

00:02:15.368 --> 00:02:17.504
better than the Ukrainians were

00:02:17.504 --> 00:02:18.605
hiding in the root cellar.

00:02:20.073 --> 00:02:21.241
So now we're in the big

00:02:21.241 --> 00:02:23.309
field behind Olga's house.

00:02:23.309 --> 00:02:25.078
They're still foxholes back here

00:02:25.078 --> 00:02:25.912
And this is one of them.

00:02:25.912 --> 00:02:27.514
You sort of just walk amidst

00:02:27.514 --> 00:02:29.282
all of this roughage.

00:02:29.282 --> 00:02:30.216
And this is one of the main

00:02:30.216 --> 00:02:33.253
Russian foxholes that's still here

00:02:33.253 --> 00:02:34.621
and go inside.

00:02:34.621 --> 00:02:35.155
We understand

00:02:35.155 --> 00:02:37.223
this has been cleaned up of mines

00:02:37.223 --> 00:02:38.324
and other things.

00:02:38.324 --> 00:02:40.660
And I'll just take you inside

00:02:43.796 --> 00:02:44.564
well,

00:02:46.166 --> 00:02:47.100
you can see the Russians.

00:02:47.100 --> 00:02:47.867
They really are.

00:02:47.867 --> 00:02:49.369
They really dug it out in here.

00:02:49.369 --> 00:02:50.837
Still see the Russian

00:02:50.837 --> 00:02:53.706
Marie, the mills, what they were using to

00:02:53.806 --> 00:02:54.407
to cook.

00:02:54.407 --> 00:02:55.341
They built a makeshift

00:02:55.341 --> 00:02:56.109
stove here

00:02:56.109 --> 00:02:57.410
even and still,

00:02:57.410 --> 00:02:59.679
as I mentioned, these makeshift chimneys.

00:02:59.812 --> 00:03:02.282
And this one was pretty sophisticated.

00:03:02.282 --> 00:03:02.715
Olga says

00:03:02.715 --> 00:03:04.083
this is one of the nicest foxholes

00:03:04.083 --> 00:03:05.418
that the Russians built.

00:03:05.418 --> 00:03:06.486
And I just want to say again,

00:03:06.486 --> 00:03:07.921
the Russians were living a lot

00:03:07.921 --> 00:03:10.056
better than the Ukrainians.

00:03:10.056 --> 00:03:10.890
But this is the evidence

00:03:10.890 --> 00:03:11.991
up here in Kiev region,

00:03:11.991 --> 00:03:14.194
of course, is on the front lines.

00:03:14.194 --> 00:03:16.563
Ukrainians are camping in the woods.

00:03:16.563 --> 00:03:18.031
Entrenched in these positions,

00:03:18.031 --> 00:03:20.700
embedded in the woods, fighting even now

00:03:21.100 --> 00:03:22.235
to try to free their country.

00:03:25.538 --> 00:03:26.639
As we got ready to leave

00:03:26.639 --> 00:03:27.840
all this house today,

00:03:27.840 --> 00:03:30.243
she turned to cut some flowers

00:03:30.677 --> 00:03:32.111
and she brought them to me,

00:03:32.111 --> 00:03:34.080
asking me to take them to her son.

00:03:34.080 --> 00:03:36.082
Ivan's grave nearby.

00:03:36.082 --> 00:03:38.151
It was meaningful to me to be asked

00:03:38.718 --> 00:03:40.720
because it mattered to her.

00:03:41.521 --> 00:03:43.790
And we went and there we saw

00:03:43.790 --> 00:03:47.560
Ivan as a boy and then as a soldier.

00:03:48.161 --> 00:03:50.830
And I laid his mother's beautiful flowers

00:03:51.030 --> 00:03:52.532
from her garden.

00:03:52.532 --> 00:03:55.268
And we thought about this one precious

00:03:56.102 --> 00:03:56.970
lost life

